Problem Statement : Given an integer array, find the subarray with the largest sum and return the sum of the elements present in that subarray.

Brute Force Approach: 
Main idea: Find all possible subarrays, calculate the sum of each one, and store the largest sum in maxi.
- i — starting index of the subarray.
- j — ending index of the subarray.
- k — traverses the selected subarray and adds its elements.
- sum — sum of the current subarray.
- maxi — maximum sum found so far.

Code:
for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
{
    for (j = i; j < n; j++)
    {
        sum = 0;

        for (k = i; k <= j; k++)
            sum += arr[k];

        maxi = max(sum, maxi);
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n^3)
Space Complexity: (O(1)

